### Lab 7 demonstration — open in IntelliJ IDEA and press ▶ next to a request.
### The application must be running on port 8080.

### 3. The collection: 200, a JSON array of BookResponse
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books

### 3. One book: 200, HAL with _links (variant 7: self, books, citation)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/1

### 4. Create: 201 Created + Location header + the new book in the body
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Pro Spring 6",
  "author": "Iuliana Cosmina",
  "year": 2023,
  "genre": "PROGRAMMING",
  "available": true,
  "publishedOn": "2023-03-01"
}

### 5. Follow the Location of the created book (id 5 on a fresh start)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/5

### 9. Create the same book again: 409 Conflict, application/problem+json
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Pro Spring 6",
  "author": "Iuliana Cosmina",
  "year": 2023,
  "genre": "PROGRAMMING"
}

### 8. An empty title: 400, problem detail produced by ResponseEntityExceptionHandler
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "author": "Iuliana Cosmina",
  "year": 2023,
  "genre": "PROGRAMMING"
}

### Replace: 200 (PUT writes every field; createdAt is kept by the server)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/books/5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Pro Spring 6, 2nd printing",
  "author": "Iuliana Cosmina",
  "year": 2023,
  "genre": "PROGRAMMING",
  "available": false,
  "publishedOn": "2023-03-01"
}

### 6. Delete: 204 No Content
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/5

### 6. The same DELETE again: 404 with a problem detail
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/5

### 7. A missing book: 404, application/problem+json — type, title, status, detail, instance
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/999

### 11. The OpenAPI document (Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html)
GET http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs
